<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on March 4.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on March 4.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Saigon 4		SLD Feb 27	12,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pan Korea	     SLD Feb 27	14,700	S.Korea</p>
<p>Al Tabith	     SLD Feb 02	13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Hua Shan		SLD Feb 02	14,000	Iran</p>
<p>Orient Express	SLD Feb 26	 1,000	Cambodia</p>
<p>Kai Manu		SLD Mar 03	12,600	S. Korea</p>
<p>Ban Jiang	     SLD Feb 27	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pradu		   SLD Feb 27	 3,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Great Power	   SLD Mar 03	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Lyong Gun Bong	SLD Feb 27	 6,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Zi Yun		  SLD Feb 28	 6,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Yulin		   SLD Mar 02	 8,000	Japan</p>
<p>He Jiang		SLD Feb 28	 4,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Bang Yeerua	   SLD Mar 03	 6,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Mani II		 SLD Mar 01	 2,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangkhunnon	   SLD Feb 28	 6,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Great Universe	ETD mar 03	14,300	Indonesia</p>
<p>Huang Hua	     N/A		 14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Feng Zhan	     ETD Mar 06	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Golden Glint	  N/A		  6,300	Indonesia</p>
<p>Myohyang 3	    ETD Mar 09	13,900	Indonesia</p>
<p>Nocholas I.K.	 N/A		 15,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Tropical Damsel     ETD Mar 03	 8,000	Japan</p>
<p>Feng Tao		ETD Mar 11	13,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Delight		 ETD Mar 04	 5,850	Indonesia</p>
<p>Marina Lauri	  ETD Mar 09	10,000	China</p>
<p>Han Chaun	     ETD Mar 08	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Progress Excellence ETD Mar 12	13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Kum Gang		ETD Mar 06	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Lisson Leader	 N/A		 14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Hyoksin		 ARRD Mar 02     13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
